      "title": "START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Open-H3 Regenerate 2K — Ref2VA to 2K\n**References → 1344×768 Ref2VA draft → 2560×1440 FL2VA refine.** The draft is 124 frames at 24 fps (about 5.17 s). Its generated soundtrack is saved with both videos.\n\n1. Upload an image in **<Picture 1> reference**; `reference.png` is a placeholder. The example prompts describe a red fox. Edit **both prompts** to match your subject and scene.\n2. The **draft prompt** uses `<Picture 1>` to preserve appearance. The **refine prompt** describes the scene directly, without reference tags or attached media. References shape the draft; the baseline refine follows its latent and a fresh text-only encoding.\n3. Draft model: **fused Ref2VA turbo8**, 8 steps, er_sde, CFG 1. It has its own model loader and needs no extra Turbo LoRA. Refine model: **FL2VA** with the Open-H3 merged LoRA and Sharp curves, 3 Euler steps, CFG 1.\n4. More references: connect images to the native Ref2VA node's growing image inputs; connect video frames at 24 fps and their matching soundtrack to its video/audio inputs, or connect standalone audio. Keep the prompt's `<Picture N>`, `<Video N>` and `<Audio N>` labels aligned with the inputs.\n\nThe selected fused Ref2VA checkpoint is the locally installed preset used for the comparison. This repository does not include or download it. If you use another Ref2VA model, select it and use its recommended sampling settings; the eight-step settings here were tested only with this preset.\n\n**Refine policy:** Text-only baseline; references are used only by the draft.\n**Noise:** *Sigmas* `start_sigma` **0**. Zero selects the release recipe (0.909375); 0.8 redraws less. The four-way comparison is complete; human selection of the shipping default is pending.\n\nAt 0.8 the final step (sigma 0.48) falls below the existing Sol-Attn cutoff and runs dense. The release schedule keeps eligible attention sparse in all three steps. In one public-demo comparison, 0.8 preserved more headdress structure and retained references showed no clear benefit; all four variants still changed facial details. See `docs/ref2va-workflow.md` in the repository for the comparison and limitations.\n\nAudio is held as encoded silence inside the refiner. The exported soundtrack is decoded from the generated draft, not copied from a reference recording. The refined latent and that soundtrack are saved before decoding for recovery with **Decode Saved Latent**.\n\n**Time:** Measured on RTX PRO 5000 Blackwell 72 GB / Windows, 124 frames: full release-sigma workflow (draft + 2K) **7m43s** including first model initialization. Reused-draft runs: references kept / release **2m59s**, text-only / 0.8 **4m43s**, references kept / 0.8 **4m53s**. These are single-run timings with different initialization costs, not equivalent cold/warm benchmarks.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#2a2a2a",
      "bgcolor": "#353535"
    },
