        "integrated_multimodal_description:\n[Shot 1] From 0.0 s to 5.2 s, a low tracking shot at eye level with shallow depth of field follows a red fox as it trots left to right through fresh, knee-deep snow in a quiet birch forest at golden hour. The fox has a thick orange-red winter coat, a white chest and throat, black legs and black-tipped ears, and a bushy tail with a white tip; its breath steams in the cold air. Each paw sinks into untouched powder and kicks up fine crystals that sparkle in the low sun, its guard hairs catching warm backlight. Birch trunks with peeling white bark pass in soft focus behind it. The camera glides alongside at a steady pace. The visual style is photoreal live action.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSnow crunches softly under each paw, wind moves through the bare branches, and a bird calls in the distance.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
